{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
If my words did [G]glow with the gold of [C]sunshine
And my tunes were played on the harp [G]unstrung,
Would you hear my voice come thru the [C]music?
Would you [G]hold it [D]near [C]as it were your [G]own?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It's a hand-me-down, the thoughts are broken;
Perhaps they're better left unsung.
I don't know, don't really care.
Let there be songs to fill the air.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Ripple in still [D]water, when there [G]is no pebble [C]tossed,
Nor [A7]wind to [D]blow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Reach out your hand if your cup be empty,
If your cup is full may it be again.
Let it be known there is a fountain
That was not made by the hands of men.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
There is a road, no simple highway,
Between the dawn and the dark of night,
And if you go, no one may follow,
That path is for your steps alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Ripple in still water, when there is no pebble tossed,
Nor wind to blow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
You who choose to lead must follow,
But if you fall, you fall alone.
If you should stand, then who's to guide you?
If I knew the way I would take you home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
La da da da da,La da da da da etc
{end_of_verse}
